{"id":"U16","title":"John Todd's Eco-Machine","titleZh":"约翰·托德的生态机器","paras":[{"id":"U16-P1","sentences":[{"id":"U16-P1-S1","hard":false,"text":"When John Todd was a child, he loved to explore the woods around his house, observing how nature solved problems."},{"id":"U16-P1-S2","hard":false,"text":"A dirty stream, for example, often became clear after flowing through plants and along rocks where tiny creatures lived."},{"id":"U16-P1-S3","hard":true,"text":"When he got older, John started to wonder if this process could be used to clean up the messes people were making."}],"zh":"约翰·托德小时候喜欢探索家周围的树林，观察大自然如何解决问题。例如，一条污浊的小溪在流经植物和微小生物栖息的岩石后，往往会变得清澈。长大后，约翰开始思考，这个过程是否可以用来清理人们制造的混乱。"},{"id":"U16-P2","sentences":[{"id":"U16-P2-S1","hard":false,"text":"After studying agriculture, medicine, and fisheries in college, John went back to observing nature and asking questions."},{"id":"U16-P2-S2","hard":false,"text":"Why can certain plants trap harmful bacteria?"},{"id":"U16-P2-S3","hard":false,"text":"Which kinds of fish can eat cancer-causing chemicals?"},{"id":"U16-P2-S4","hard":true,"text":"With the right combination of animals and plants, he figured, maybe he could clean up waste the way nature did."},{"id":"U16-P2-S5","hard":false,"text":"He decided to build what he would later call an eco-machine."}],"zh":"在大学学习了农业、医学和渔业之后，约翰回到观察自然和提出问题。为什么某些植物能够捕获有害细菌？哪些鱼类可以吃掉致癌化学物质？他想，有了合适的动植物组合，也许他可以像大自然那样清理废物。他决定建造一台他后来称之为\"生态机器\"的装置。"},{"id":"U16-P3","sentences":[{"id":"U16-P3-S1","hard":false,"text":"The task John set for himself was to remove harmful substances from some sludge."},{"id":"U16-P3-S2","hard":false,"text":"First, he constructed a series of clear fiberglass tanks connected to each other."},{"id":"U16-P3-S3","hard":false,"text":"Then he went around to local ponds and streams and brought back some plants and animals."},{"id":"U16-P3-S4","hard":false,"text":"He placed them in the tanks and waited."},{"id":"U16-P3-S5","hard":false,"text":"Little by little, these different kinds of life got used to one another and formed their own ecosystem."},{"id":"U16-P3-S6","hard":false,"text":"After a few weeks, John added the sludge."}],"zh":"约翰给自己设定的任务是从一些污泥中去除有害物质。首先，他建造了一系列相互连接的透明玻璃纤维水箱。然后他到当地的池塘和溪流中去，带回了一些动植物。他把它们放进水箱里等待。渐渐地，这些不同种类的生命相互适应，形成了自己的生态系统。几周后，约翰加入了污泥。"},{"id":"U16-P4","sentences":[{"id":"U16-P4-S1","hard":false,"text":"He was amazed at the results."},{"id":"U16-P4-S2","hard":false,"text":"The plants and animals in the eco-machine took the sludge as food and began to eat it!"},{"id":"U16-P4-S3","hard":false,"text":"Within weeks, it had all been digested, and all that was left was pure water."}],"zh":"他对结果感到惊讶。生态机器中的动植物把污泥当作食物，开始吃它！几周之内，污泥全部被消化，剩下的只有纯净的水。"},{"id":"U16-P5","sentences":[{"id":"U16-P5-S1","hard":false,"text":"Over the years, John has taken on many big jobs."},{"id":"U16-P5-S2","hard":false,"text":"He developed a greenhouse-like facility that treated sewage from 1,600 homes in South Burlington."},{"id":"U16-P5-S3","hard":false,"text":"He also designed an eco-machine to clean canal water in Fuzhou, a city in southeast China."}],"zh":"多年来，约翰承担了许多大项目。他开发了一个类似温室的设施，处理南伯灵顿1600户家庭的污水。他还设计了一台生态机器来清洁中国东南部城市福州的运河水。"},{"id":"U16-P6","sentences":[{"id":"U16-P6-S1","hard":false,"text":"\"Ecological design\" is the name John gives to what he does."},{"id":"U16-P6-S2","hard":false,"text":"\"Life on Earth is kind of a box of spare parts for the inventor,\" he says."},{"id":"U16-P6-S3","hard":false,"text":"\"You put organisms in new relationships and observe what's happening."},{"id":"U16-P6-S4","hard":false,"text":"Then you let these new systems develop their own ways to self-repair.\""}],"zh":"\"生态设计\"是约翰对自己所从事工作的命名。\"地球上的生命对发明者来说就像一盒备件，\"他说。\"你把生物体放入新的关系中，观察正在发生什么。然后你让这些新系统以它们自己的方式发展自我修复。\""}],"words":[{"id":"U16-W01","lemma":"explore","surface":"explore","pos":"v.","zh":"探索; 探险; 探究","sent":"U16-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"explore the woods","zh":"探索树林"},{"en":"explore possibilities","zh":"探索可能性"}]},{"id":"U16-W02","lemma":"wood","surface":"woods","pos":"n.","zh":"树林; 森林; 木材","sent":"U16-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"in the woods","zh":"在树林里"}]},{"id":"U16-W03","lemma":"observe","surface":"observing","pos":"v.","zh":"观察; 遵守; 庆祝","sent":"U16-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"observe nature","zh":"观察自然"},{"en":"observe the rules","zh":"遵守规则"}]},{"id":"U16-W04","lemma":"stream","surface":"stream","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 小溪; 流 v. 流动; 流出","sent":"U16-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"a dirty stream","zh":"一条污浊的小溪"},{"en":"stream of","zh":"一连串..."}]},{"id":"U16-W05","lemma":"example","surface":"example","pos":"n.","zh":"例子; 榜样","sent":"U16-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"for example","zh":"例如"},{"en":"set an example","zh":"树立榜样"}]},{"id":"U16-W06","lemma":"flow","surface":"flowing","pos":"v. / n.","zh":"v. 流动; 流出 n. 流动; 流量","sent":"U16-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"flow through","zh":"流经..."}]},{"id":"U16-W07","lemma":"plant","surface":"plants","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 植物; 工厂 v. 种植; 放置","sent":"U16-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"flow through plants","zh":"流经植物"}]},{"id":"U16-W08","lemma":"rock","surface":"rocks","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 岩石; 摇滚乐 v. 摇晃; 使震惊","sent":"U16-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"along rocks","zh":"沿着岩石"}]},{"id":"U16-W09","lemma":"tiny","surface":"tiny","pos":"adj.","zh":"微小的; 极小的","sent":"U16-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"tiny creatures","zh":"微小生物"}]},{"id":"U16-W10","lemma":"process","surface":"process","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 过程; 进程; 工序 v. 处理; 加工","sent":"U16-P1-S3","phrases":[{"en":"natural process","zh":"自然过程"},{"en":"in the process of","zh":"在...过程中"}]},{"id":"U16-W11","lemma":"mess","surface":"messes","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 混乱; 脏乱; 困境 v. 弄乱; 搞砸","sent":"U16-P1-S3","phrases":[{"en":"clean up the mess","zh":"清理混乱"},{"en":"in a mess","zh":"一团糟"}]},{"id":"U16-W12","lemma":"agriculture","surface":"agriculture","pos":"n.","zh":"农业; 农学","sent":"U16-P2-S1","phrases":[{"en":"study agriculture","zh":"学习农业"}]},{"id":"U16-W13","lemma":"medicine","surface":"medicine","pos":"n.","zh":"医学; 药; 药物","sent":"U16-P2-S1","phrases":[{"en":"study me